[size=4][i]More of Skyrim for your magic tattoos.[/i][/size]

[size=5][b]Description[/b][/size]

This patch adds base game conditions and effects to [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/180775]Magic Tattoos Framework[/url] (MTF), on top of the ones built into MTF. A tattoo tier can show once the player has picked a hundred locks, under a full moon, on Saturalia, while they have a bounty in the hold they're standing in, while hidden in a shadow, at a forge, with Flames in hand, or for a few seconds after a kill or a cast of Fireball. A tier can also grant night vision, shorten shout cooldowns, cure diseases, keep the Well Rested bonus, set the actor's facial expression, calm nearby enemies, prevent fall damage, change the weather, grant experience, wrap the actor in one of 80 magic auras, cast any spell on the actor, or give them a spell aura that heals or burns their own side every second.

It adds a [b]Skyrim[/b] plugin to MTF's menu and to [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/196803]Magic Tattoos UI[/url]. It doesn't edit any game records.

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/180775]Magic Tattoos Framework[/url] 0.7.0 or later, and its requirements
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/13048]PapyrusUtil SE[/url]
[*]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/22854]powerofthree's Papyrus Extender[/url] for Hidden, Diseased, Cure disease, Calm enemies, and the nearby actors of Spell aura. Without it, the first four do nothing, and Spell aura only reaches the actor and the player.
[*]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/196803]Magic Tattoos Framework - SKSE UI[/url], an editor in the SKSE Menu Framework menu, with live previews. It makes setting up tiers with these conditions and effects far easier, and 1.8.0 or later picks the spell for Cast a spell and Spell aura from a searchable list. With 1.8.3 or later, those spells are as strong as if whoever applied the tattoo cast them. With 1.8.6 or later, Spell aura fire-and-forget hits land at half strength, and the picker hides awkward spells unless you turn them back on.
[/list]

Dawnguard and Dragonborn come with Skyrim Special Edition. The connector uses a few of their forms: the Aetherium Forge, the Staff Enchanter, Solstheim's bounty, the Black Book perk behind No fall damage, and some of the magic auras.

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Install with your mod manager and enable [font=Courier New]MTF_Plugin_Skyrim.esp[/font]. It is ESL-flagged and only lists [font=Courier New]Skyrim.esm[/font] and [font=Courier New]MagicTattoosFramework.esp[/font] as masters, so it can go anywhere after MTF.

[size=5][b]Conditions[/b][/size]

Conditions marked "player" are always false on an NPC, because the game keeps that information for the player only.

[list]
[*][b]Statistic[/b]: (player) a General Stats value has reached 1 to 10,000. There are 88 to pick from, such as locks picked, items stolen, days as a vampire, and dragon souls collected
[*][b]Moon phase[/b]: the moons are in one of the eight phases, or in any waxing or any waning phase
[*][b]In darkness[/b]: the light on the actor is below a level, 40 by default
[*][b]Season[/b]: it is winter, spring, summer, or autumn
[*][b]Holiday[/b]: it is one of the 22 holidays on the in-game calendar, or any of them
[*][b]Bounty in this hold[/b]: (player) the player has at least this much bounty in the hold they are in
[*][b]Wanted anywhere[/b]: (player) the player has at least this much bounty in any hold, Solstheim included
[*][b]Hidden[/b]: the actor is sneaking and no one nearby has detected them. The player's followers don't count
[*][b]Sitting[/b]: the actor sits in furniture
[*][b]Sleeping[/b]: the actor is asleep
[*][b]At a crafting station[/b]: the actor is using a forge, workbench, grindstone, smelter, tanning rack, cooking pot, alchemy lab, enchanter, or any of them
[*][b]Diseased[/b]: the actor has any disease, Sanguinare Vampiris included
[*][b]Just made a kill[/b]: (player) the player has killed at least 1 to 20 people, animals, creatures, undead, daedra, or automatons in the last 1 to 120 seconds
[*][b]Just leveled up[/b]: for 1 to 600 seconds after the actor gains a level
[*][b]Spell in hand[/b]: the actor has a spell equipped in either hand, drawn or not, whose name is or contains one of a list
[*][b]Just cast a spell[/b]: for 1 to 120 seconds after the actor casts a spell whose name is or contains one of a list
[*][b]Spell school in hand[/b]: the actor has an Alteration, Conjuration, Destruction, Illusion, or Restoration spell equipped in either hand, or a spell of any of them
[*][b]Just cast from a spell school[/b]: for 1 to 120 seconds after the actor casts a spell of that spell school, or of any spell school
[/list]

The General Stats page has no "dragons killed", so use Dragon souls collected for that. The moon phase follows the moons drawn in the sky: a 24-day cycle with three days per phase, starting full. Seasons go by month: Evening Star to Sun's Dawn is winter, First Seed to Second Seed is spring, Midyear to Last Seed is summer, and Hearthfire to Frostfall is autumn.

Bounty in this hold uses the hold of the actor's current location. Unnamed wilderness has no location, so between named places the condition is false even though guards there would arrest you. Just made a kill and Just leveled up learn the current count the first time MTF checks them after a load, so a kill made before that doesn't count.

Spell in hand and Just cast a spell take spell names as they appear in game, in any case, with commas between several: [font=Courier New]Flames, Frostbite, Sparks[/font] matches any of the three. Match picks whether the name must be the whole spell name (is) or only part of it (contains): with contains, [font=Courier New]fire[/font] matches Fireball, Firebolt, and Fire Rune, and also any spell from another mod with "fire" anywhere in its name. A game in another language, or a mod that renames a spell, needs the name it shows. Pair Spell in hand with MTF's Weapon Drawn condition to need the hands raised. For the player, Just cast a spell counts every spell the game casts, powers included, but not scrolls or staffs. For an NPC it counts spells cast from either hand, starting from the first time MTF checks the condition on them, so a cast before that doesn't count.

Spell school in hand and Just cast from a spell school go by the spell's costliest effect, the same spell school the game gives the skill experience to, and work with spells from other mods without any setup. Powers have no spell school, so only Just cast a spell can match them, by name and on the player. The two cast conditions watch NPCs the same way.

[size=5][b]Effects[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Night vision[/b] ([i]while shown[/i]): (player) the Night Eye vision
[*][b]Shout recovery[/b] ([i]while shown[/i]): shout cooldowns last 10 to 300% as long as usual
[*][b]Cure disease[/b] ([i]once[/i]): cures every disease the actor has
[*][b]Rested bonus[/b] ([i]while shown[/i]): keeps Rested, Well Rested, or Lover's Comfort on the actor
[*][b]Facial mood[/b] ([i]while shown[/i]): holds a neutral, angry, fearful, happy, sad, surprised, puzzled, or disgusted expression at 0 to 100% strength
[*][b]Calm enemies[/b] ([i]once[/i]): everyone within 5 to 100 metres who is hostile to the actor, or fighting them, stops fighting
[*][b]No fall damage[/b] ([i]while shown[/i]): (player) falling does no harm
[*][b]Change the weather[/b] ([i]once[/i]): (player) the weather turns clear, cloudy, foggy, rainy, stormy, snowy, or to a blizzard
[*][b]Grant experience[/b] ([i]once[/i]): (player) gains 1 to 100% of the experience their current level needs
[*][b]Magic aura[/b] ([i]while shown[/i]): the actor wears one of 80 visual effects, listed below
[*][b]Cast a spell[/b] ([i]while shown[/i]): any spell lands on the actor (fire-and-forget at effect duration or cast time, whichever is longer; concentration every second at about ten seconds of strength; self buffs once); concentration always costs magicka, other spells optionally (applier only when set; wearer only when none)
[*][b]Cast an aura[/b] ([i]while shown[/i]): a spell lands on actors within 1 to 50 metres who share the wearer's side (not enemies of them): neither hits the wearer; fire-and-forget at half strength on effect duration or cast time, concentration every second at about ten seconds of strength (applier only when set; wearer only when none)
[/list]

How the effects behave:

[list]
[*][b]Night vision.[/b] Casting Night Eye while the tattoo shows and then letting it run out also ends the tattoo's vision until the next load. Toggling the tier back on restores it.
[*][b]Shout recovery.[/b] Several tiers add up, and the multiplier never goes below 5%.
[*][b]Cure disease.[/b] Like a Cure Disease potion, it also cures Sanguinare Vampiris before it turns into vampirism.
[*][b]Rested bonus.[/b] The bonus is put back every few seconds if sleeping replaces it or it expires. A bonus the actor already had when the tier appeared stays when the tier goes.
[*][b]Facial mood.[/b] The most recently shown mood wins, and it is put back after dialogue or combat changes the face.
[*][b]Calm enemies.[/b] Bandits, draugr, and other enemies that are always hostile may attack again.
[*][b]No fall damage.[/b] This uses the perk from the Black Book "The Hidden Twilight". If the player has already earned that perk, it stays when the tier goes.
[*][b]Change the weather.[/b] The new weather lasts until the climate changes it again on its own.
[*][b]Grant experience.[/b] The amount is a share of the current level, so 10% is always a tenth of a level, at level 5 or level 50. It goes to the character level, not to any skill, and is granted each time the tier appears.
[*][b]Magic aura.[/b] These are the game's own spell and power visuals, picked from the ones MTF's Shader effect doesn't already offer. Different auras stack. Two tiers with the same aura show it once, and it stays until both stop. The game doesn't save auras, so after a load each one comes back within a few seconds. When the tier stops it removes its aura from the actor, including the same visual from a real spell: Oakflesh cast while an Oakflesh tier shows loses its glow early when the tier goes.
[*][b]Cast a spell and Cast an aura.[/b] These work with any spell, from the game or from other mods. Pick it from the searchable list in Magic Tattoos UI (awkward spells such as cloaks, wards, and summons are hidden unless you turn on Show awkward spells). In MTF's own menu, type it as [font=Courier New]Plugin.esp|0xFormID[/font], such as [font=Courier New]Skyrim.esm|0x012FCD[/font] for Flames, or as the name of a spell the player knows. The spell's effects land straight on the target, with no casting animation or projectile, so pair a Magic aura with it for something to see. With Magic Tattoos UI 1.8.3 or later, the spell is as strong as if whoever applied the tattoo cast it, with their perks and Fortify (School) potions; without it, those may not count. Cast a spell keeps hitting the wearer while the tier is shown: fire-and-forget spells wait for their effect duration when they have one (Fear and similar), otherwise use cast time (Firebolt), at least half a second; concentration such as Flames every second at about ten seconds of strength when UI 1.8.6 or later is present; self buffs such as Oakflesh land once. Cast an aura uses the same fire-and-forget spacing on nearby actors (half strength with UI 1.8.6+); concentration pulses every second at the same ten-second strength. A spell counts as harmful when its main effect is hostile, as with Flames or Frostbite. Both helpful and harmful auras hit everyone nearby who isn't an enemy of the wearer; neither hits the wearer. So a Flames hex on a bandit burns the bandits around them, and a Healing aura on that same bandit heals those bandits. The tattoo's own wearer counts as having applied it, unless a mod such as Magic Tattoos Tactical says otherwise. The game treats the applier as the caster, so the damage, the anger it causes, kill credit, and skill experience go to them. Concentration always costs one second of the spell's magicka per pulse (one payment for a whole aura ring); other spells use the pay option when it is on. Magicka comes only from whoever applied the tattoo when that actor is recorded; the wearer is never charged as a fallback. With no applier recorded, the wearer pays. When the payer can't afford it, the pulse pauses and resumes when magicka recovers.
[/list]

The auras, by group:

[list]
[*][b]Armor and elements[/b]: Oakflesh, Ironflesh, Shield spell, Shield Charge, Lightning cloak, Frost (light), Frost spikes, Ice Form, Steam, Webbed, Chaurus poison
[*][b]Enchantments[/b]: Enchanted glow (red, blue, purple, green), Fire, Frost, and Shock enchantment, Elemental Fury, Bound weapon, Potion glow (fire, frost, magicka, shock, poison)
[*][b]Illusion[/b]: Illusion (positive, negative), Fear, Paralysis, Berserker rage, Nightmare, Kyne's Peace, Animal Allegiance, Disguise
[*][b]Absorb[/b]: Absorb magicka, Absorb stamina, Dragon soul absorb, Greybeard power
[*][b]Ghosts and shadows[/b]: Ghost (violet), Wolf spirit, Call of Valor, Ghost (College of Winterhold), Nightingale spirit, Nightingale (corrupted), Nightingale shadow, Boethiah's shadow
[*][b]Racial powers and healing[/b]: Dragonskin, Highborn, Command Animal, Ancestor's Wrath, Histskin, Adrenaline Rush, Healing circle, Mystic healing, Water breathing
[*][b]Daedra and legends[/b]: Azura (radiant, corrupted), Boethiah, Sovngarde, Ancano's power, Flame Atronach
[*][b]Dawnguard[/b]: Sun fire cloak, Sun fire, Soul Cairn ghost, Soul Cairn, Mistform, Drain Vitality, Auriel's fire
[*][b]Dragonborn[/b]: Miraak's magic, Miraak's smoke, Dragon Aspect 1 to 3, Ash Shell, Ash Guardian, Whirlwind cloak, Mora's Grasp, Omen of danger, Apocrypha magic, Seeker
[/list]

Some were made for one creature or scene and may look different on a person.

[size=5][b]Resetting[/b][/size]

If a change from Shout recovery, Rested bonus, Facial mood, Night vision, No fall damage, Magic aura, or Spell aura ever stays after its tattoo is gone, you can undo everything those effects have changed. Open the console and enter:

[code]setpqv MTF_Plugin_Skyrim ResetOnLoad 1[/code]

Then save and load that save. The player and every actor MTF tracks lose those changes, and the Papyrus log shows [font=Courier New][MTF_Plugin_Skyrim] reset N actor(s)[/font]. The setting turns itself off again, so later loads don't reset. A tier that is still showing comes back the next time it starts.

[size=5][b]Uninstalling[/b][/size]

Take off any tattoo whose tiers use Shout recovery, Rested bonus, Facial mood, Night vision, No fall damage, Magic aura, or Spell aura, so their changes are undone, or use the reset above. Then save, quit, and disable the plugin.

If you play on without the plugin and later add it back, its leftover changes are undone on the first load, and any tier still showing applies again a few seconds later.

[size=5][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

The Papyrus log ([font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/Logs/Script/Papyrus.0.log[/font]) should show [font=Courier New][MTF_Main] Registered 'proteux-mtf.skyrim'[/font] a few seconds after loading a save. If it doesn't, check that [font=Courier New]MTF_Plugin_Skyrim.esp[/font] is enabled and loads after [font=Courier New]MagicTattoosFramework.esp[/font]. Errors mentioning [font=Courier New]PO3_SKSEFunctions[/font] mean Papyrus Extender is missing.

[url=https://github.com/proteux/skyrim-magic-tattoo-connectors/blob/main/connectors/skyrim/TESTING.md]TESTING.md[/url] walks through checking each condition and effect in game.

